  "style": {
    "id": "schlieren",
    "name": "Schlieren",
    "description": "Invisible air made visible: a big round mirror on an optics bench in a dim lab, a candle in front of it, a razor blade on a micrometer stand at the focus. With the blade out the mirror is an even ivory disc showing only the candle and its flame; slide the blade into the focus and the disc dims to grey and the 'still' air above the flame appears as a rising, rolling plume drawn in light and dark. One shader on the disc: a procedural plume density (closed form of position and t: rising, widening, rolling, pushed sideways by a breath puff in closed form) and the picture is its sideways derivative ∂n/∂x — what a vertical knife edge really selects.",
